 "Two works from this stretch follow — <i>TV Cello</i> and <i>Electronic Superhighway</i>. Neither was in the original deck; both are learning objectives in the lesson plan, so slides were built for them.": "這一段還有兩件作品接在後面 — 〈電視大提琴〉與〈電子高速公路〉。原本的簡報兩件都沒有；兩件都是教案裡的學習目標，所以替它們做了投影片。",
 "TV Cello": "電視大提琴",
 "Nam June Paik, <i>TV Cello</i>, 1971 — three television sets, one string, and a bow": "白南準，〈電視大提琴〉，1971 — 三台電視、一根弦，和一把弓",
 "It is a cello you cannot really play. So what is it for?": "這是一把你其實彈不了的大提琴。那它是用來做什麼的？",
 "Three television cabinets stacked into the shape of a cello, with a real string and bridge across them.": "三個電視機殼疊成一把大提琴的形狀，上面架著一根真的弦與琴橋。",
 "The cellist Charlotte Moorman played it — and the screens showed her playing it, live, while she played.": "大提琴家夏洛特・摩爾曼演奏它 — 而螢幕上即時播出的，就是她正在演奏它的畫面。",
 "They worked together for twenty years. She also performed wearing television sets.": "他們合作了二十年。她也曾經身上穿戴著電視機演出。",
 "The performer, the instrument and the broadcast all become one object.": "演奏者、樂器與播送，全部變成同一個物件。",
 "ASK first. The useful answer: it is not a joke instrument, it is a feedback loop you can hold between your knees.": "先問。有用的答案是：它不是一件搞笑樂器，而是一個你可以夾在兩膝之間的回饋迴圈。",
 "Moorman is the reason these works exist as performances rather than sculptures, and she is routinely left out of the story. Name her.": "摩爾曼是這些作品之所以是「表演」而不是「雕塑」的原因，而她經常被排除在這個故事之外。請把她的名字說出來。",
 "She was arrested in New York in 1967 for performing one of their pieces topless, and became known as the “topless cellist” — which is how a serious avant-garde musician gets remembered for the wrong thing.": "1967 年她在紐約因為上空演出他們的一件作品而被逮捕，從此被稱為「上空大提琴家」 — 一位認真的前衛音樂家，就這樣因為錯誤的理由被記住。",
 "The link to make: this is {{closedcircuit}} again, like <i>TV Buddha</i>, but with a living body inside the loop. That is the bridge to the whole second half of today.": "要建立的連結：這又是{{closedcircuit}}，跟〈電視佛陀〉一樣，只是這次迴圈裡有一具活生生的身體。那就是通往今天整個後半段的橋。",
 "NOTE: this slide is not in Vicky’s original deck. The photograph is freely licensed — see the README.": "注意：這一頁不在 Vicky 原本的簡報裡。這張照片是自由授權 — 詳見 README。",
 "Electronic Superhighway": "電子高速公路",
 "He used the phrase “electronic superhighway” in 1974 — twenty years before the internet arrived. What did he think was coming?": "他在 1974 年就用了「電子高速公路」這個詞 — 比網際網路出現早了二十年。他當時認為什麼正在到來？",
 "Nam June Paik, <i>Electronic Superhighway: Continental U.S., Alaska, Hawaii</i>, 1995 — the Washington, D.C. state, with its closed-circuit camera": "白南準，〈電子高速公路：美國本土、阿拉斯加、夏威夷〉，1995 — 華盛頓特區那一州，以及它的閉路攝影機",
 "The camera": "攝影機",
 "The same work from behind — scaffolding, cable and the back of the sets": "同一件作品的背面 — 鷹架、纜線，以及電視機的背後",
 "A map of the United States, fifteen metres wide, built from 336 televisions, each state outlined in neon.": "一幅十五公尺寬的美國地圖，由 336 台電視組成，每一州的輪廓都用霓虹燈勾出來。",
 "Every state plays its own footage at once. D.C. is a live camera, so you watch yourself arrive.": "每一州同時播放屬於自己的影片。華盛頓特區是一台即時攝影機，所以你會看著自己走進畫面。",
 "And from behind it is simply a rack of machines and a tangle of cable.": "而從背面看，它不過就是一排機器和一團糾纏的纜線。",
 "A country made of channels, all talking at the same time, and nobody listening to any of them.": "一個由頻道構成的國家，全部同時在說話，而沒有人在聽任何一個。",
 "ASK first. He meant the traffic, not the technology: a world saturated with channels, where everywhere is reachable and nowhere is quiet.": "先問。他指的是那些流量，不是那項科技：一個被頻道淹沒的世界，哪裡都到得了，而哪裡都不安靜。",
 "The scale is the argument. 336 screens, 50 states, all playing simultaneously — you cannot watch it, only stand in front of it.": "尺度就是論點。336 個螢幕、50 個州，全部同時播放 — 你沒辦法「看完」它，只能站在它前面。",
 "The D.C. camera is the point to land: it is {{closedcircuit}} once more, so the viewer is inside the map. Same move as <i>TV Buddha</i>, now at the size of a country.": "華盛頓特區那台攝影機是要讓他們接住的一點：這又是{{closedcircuit}}，所以觀看的人就在地圖裡面。和〈電視佛陀〉同一步棋，只是放大到一個國家的尺寸。",
 "It is in the Smithsonian American Art Museum, and the museum employs people to keep 336 ageing cathode-ray tubes alive. The work decays — which is Unit 8 arriving inside an electronic artwork.": "它收藏在史密森美國藝術博物館，而館方雇了人專門維持那 336 支老化的映像管還能亮著。這件作品正在衰敗 — 那就是第 8 單元走進了一件電子作品裡。",
 "This is a wrong-answer option in Quiz Question 4, so they need to have met it.": "這是測驗第 4 題的一個錯誤選項，所以他們必須先見過它。",
 "NOTE: this slide is not in Vicky’s original deck. Both photographs are freely licensed — see the README.": "注意：這一頁不在 Vicky 原本的簡報裡。兩張照片都是自由授權 — 詳見 README。"
